According to `GENERAL_AI_TRAINING_KNOWLEDGE.md` (General AI Training Knowledge & Systems Engineering Reference > 5. Model Weights, Checkpoints, Serialization and Runtime Artifacts > 5.6 TensorRT engines):

TensorRT builds optimized inference engines for NVIDIA hardware.

Optimizations can include:

- kernel selection;
- layer fusion;
- precision conversion;
- memory planning;
- hardware-specific execution.

#### Critical portability rule

A serialized TensorRT engine may depend on:

- GPU architecture;
- TensorRT version;
- CUDA/runtime compatibility;
- build settings.

Therefore it is not equivalent to a portable model-weight file.

